# Origin of the Injishi API (Better Auth is mounted there at /api/auth).
# Copy to .env.local to override.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# This app's own canonical origin. Used to build absolute urls in metadata, and
# read at sign-in as one entry of the allowlist below. On Vercel it falls back
# to VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, so a preview still gets a working origin —
# but a project that carries this as an EMPTY string is not unset, it is set to
# nothing, which is why the read uses `||` and not `??`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=http://localhost:3000

# The origins allowed to receive a signed-in visitor back from /sign-in
# (src/lib/redirect.ts). The operator app and the admin console have no sign-in
# screen of their own; their gates bounce here with ?redirect= pointing at an
# absolute url on their own origin, and only an EXACT match on this list is
# accepted. Anything else falls back to "/" — an open redirect from the sign-in
# screen would hand a phishing page a freshly minted session.
# The operator app is served as a zone under THIS origin (see next.config.ts
# rewrites), so its public address is this app's address. Redirect allowlists
# read this.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PMS_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Where the operator zone's own server listens; the rewrite target. Server side
# only, never shipped to the browser.
OPERATOR_APP_URL=http://localhost:3002
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Demo only. "1" lends the one seeded room (Umurage Guesthouse) to every
# catalogue property that declares no listing of its own, so the three step
# checkout can be walked end to end before hosts declare real inventory
# (F-B01). See src/data/demo-listing.ts for exactly what that claims.
# LEAVE IT UNSET anywhere a guest can reach: with it on, opening checkout from
# one property prices a room in another.
